<<~ ahu slot=`#/recut-custody-design-custody-wright-2026-10-31`>>

! recut-custody design (T20, the login suffix) — Custody-Wright, 2026-10-31

Worktree `~/.lares-scratch/recut-custody/wt` at a39b1f5df, provisioned (install, build, grammar wasm green; TiddlyWiki5 submodule by reference; `mempalace` failed: the reference path `.git/modules/mempalace` reads "not a local repository" and the fallback dials GitHub over ssh. No suite here needs it.)

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-threat-one-line`>>

!! The threat, one line
An OS host fact (git global `user.email`, read by a 2 s shell-out that swallows every error) picks WHICH custody file a vessel reads. Flip the fact and the same vessel reads as empty, and two mint paths answer "empty" by minting: a second persona root (open custody alone, no card) and, on `found`, a second place key + KEL (card-guarded, but the card guards the mint, not the uniqueness). This breaks "custody read by capability, never host".

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/authority-inputs`>>

!! Authority inputs
| input | source today | proves it | law lives | after the cut |h
| which identity dir | `larIdentityDir()` (LAR_ROOT/XDG env) | nothing: env | `vessel-paths.ts` | unchanged here (T16 injects homes) |
| which file inside it | `login` slug from git global email | nothing: host fact, wall-clock timeout | 13 call sites, each re-shells | FIXED names; no input at all |
| which face's rows | `faces/<fcid>/` via the floor index | the face index row | `vault-carriers` faceRow | unchanged; already isolates per face |
| key/KEL agree | KEL inception signs the key | `proveStandingKey` | verifier | unchanged |
| a mint may run | `openedCustody()` (+ founding-card read-back for the place key) | the card's read-back; custody holder | `generateOrLoadVesselIdentity` minting store | unchanged; uniqueness now holds by the single name + `exclusiveCustody`'s `existsSync(keyFile)` |
| root ↔ roster agree | roster line `{handleIndex, verifyingKey}` | `openCommittedRoot` names-another-key | verifier | unchanged |

Fails closed after the cut: a vessel whose files carry an old suffix reads "no key file" at boot (refusal already standing); sealed persona rows cannot open without the place key, so no root mints beside an un-founded place. Probe this in red phase (step loop), never on real custody.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-cut`>>

!! The cut (one commit after the reds)
* Names: `.vessel-key.json`, `.vessel-kel.json`, `.vessel-rotating.json`, and per face `.persona-group-root-hN.json`, `.persona-roster-hN.json`, `.persona-petnames-hN.json`, `.persona-declarations-hN.json`, `.persona-public-handles-hN.json`. (The brief named the first four families; the census found four more login-keyed persona rows.)
* `loginHint()` and the `login` parameter retire whole: nothing replaces them. `readLocalOperatorHint`'s email half burns, with its 11 dead `.catch` wrappers; `placeReadingWatch`'s "freeze the login" burns (nothing left to freeze; the KEL path stays fixed).
* `gitEmail` stops landing in the key file, the staged-rotation publish and every root row (no reader exists; a host fact written into a sealed row).
* Roster row key: UNCHANGED (`{handleIndex, verifyingKey}`; the login only ever lived in the filename).
* Founding-card read-back: UNCHANGED. It never keyed by login (`opts.placeFoundingCard` / `readBackStandsIn()`); the KEL it arms simply lands at the fixed name.
* Converges node onto the browser's shape (`browser-vessel-identity.ts` keys `vessel-key`, `persona-petnames`… with no login).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/every-reader-writer-of-a-suffixed-name`>>

